/**
 * AquaSentry ESP32 node firmware  (v5.5)
 * =====================================================================
 * Boards: ESP32 (WROOM/WROVER, dual core), ESP32-S3 (dual core), ESP32-C3 (single core).
 * Pins are chosen per chip below; every pin avoids flash/PSRAM pins, strapping pins and ADC2.
 * Builds with Espressif's Arduino core 2.0.x and 3.x (Arduino IDE or PlatformIO).
 *
 * Tasks (FreeRTOS):
 *   Telemetry (core 0): Wi-Fi, setup hotspot, web pages (/, /status.json, /setup, /update OTA),
 *                       uploads to the server, LittleFS offline buffer (1,000 readings).
 *   Sensors   (core 1 on dual-core chips, core 0 on the C3): pump, bubble check, voltammetry
 *                       scans with adaptive re-scanning, AquaNet-V3 on the chip.
 *
 * Main features
 * - Electrochemical cleaning pulse, differential ADS1115 readout, MCP4725 potential control
 * - I2C 9-pulse bus recovery, tubing anti-set reverse stroke, optical dry-run gate
 * - AquaNet-V3 trained classifier (float32 C99, 1.4 KB) + the same safety rules as the server
 * - Offline buffer on LittleFS (falls back to a small RAM buffer if the file system cannot mount)
 * - First-boot setup: if Wi-Fi is not configured or fails, a password-protected hotspot
 *   "AquaSentry-XXXX" opens with a setup page (password printed on the Serial Monitor)
 * - Readings carry the real UTC sample time (NTP) and the firmware version
 * - Optional (all off by default): HTTPS with certificate checking, battery monitor,
 *   low-power mode that deep-sleeps between tests (see "OPTIONAL FEATURES" below)
 */

